  "caption": "Quinn built six flat-pack shelves in one weekend, and by Monday the inner elbow was complaining about every mug and jar. Golfer's elbow, without a single round of golf.\n\nInner elbow pain often shows up when gripping and wrist work outpace what the tendon is ready for. Rest can calm it, but on its own it doesn't rebuild the tendon's capacity.\n\nWhat often helps: ease off the heavy gripping for a while, start with gentle wrist holds, then build strength slowly a few times a week over several weeks, and check grip size and technique on tools, racquets or clubs.\n\nTingling into the ring or little finger, numbness or hand weakness is worth getting assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
